---
description: When the user asks about past agent work, spend, or "what did we do", query the OpenBurnBar MCP instead of guessing.
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user asks about past agent work, spend, burn, or "what did we do",
use OpenBurnBar only for evidence the current client path can actually obtain:

1. Call `burnbar_resolve_capabilities` first and read the returned tool list.
2. Call `burnbar_recent_usage` for supported spend metadata.
3. On the HTTP-only marketplace path, do not send a plaintext topic to
   `burnbar_search_conversations`; it requires vault-key-derived token or
   semantic hashes from the optional local preprocessing/decrypt shim.
4. If trusted preprocessed results are available, quote them and name any
   field still sealed instead of inventing its contents.
